{"applicability":{"exclusions":[],"object_types":["goal","priority_plan","requirement","criteria","test_case","backlog_item","agent_task","agent_instruction","convergence_session","verification_matrix"],"workstreams":["all"]},"args":["object","get","POL-WORKFLOW-VDS","--context","mcp"],"artifacts":["docs/architecture/VERIFIABLE_DECOMPOSITION_SPINE.md","docs/quality/verifiable_decomposition_spine_profile.yaml","docs/quality/verifiable_decomposition_customization.yaml","docs/quality/vds_chunks.yaml"],"body":"# POL-WORKFLOW-VDS — Verifiable Decomposition Spine\n\n**Enforcement level:** blocking (`policy_type: standard`, severity critical).  \n**Scope:** Any project using this kernel/process model — not ZQK-specific.  \n**Canonical contract:** `docs/architecture/VERIFIABLE_DECOMPOSITION_SPINE.md`  \n**Spine (rigid):** `docs/quality/verifiable_decomposition_spine_profile.yaml`  \n**Customization (flexible):** `docs/quality/verifiable_decomposition_customization.yaml`\n\n## Problem this policy solves\n\nAgents can assert completion with no consequences. Natural language is not a control.\nEvery collaborative activity MUST be broken into chunks that are **independently and\nobjectively verifiable** at each stage. “Done” without re-runnable evidence is a\n**policy violation**.\n\n## Rigid spine (MUST NOT customize away)\n\nFinite stages (order fixed):\n\n1. `intent_capture` — vision, mission, goals, constraints, non-goals  \n2. `design` — requirements, criteria, test cases, backlog, agent tasks/instructions  \n3. `implement` — solution work with quality, architecture, unit evidence, review  \n4. `integrate_verify` — integration/smoke, environment, CI  \n5. `operate_release` — DevOps, security, performance, publish/ops gates  \n\n### Chunk contract (every claim of done)\n\nRequired fields: `chunk_id`, `stage`, `claim`, `rubric_ref`, `dsl_checks`,\n`evidence_refs`, `independent_verify`.\n\n- **VDS-R1:** One chunk = one independently verifiable claim. Later stages may not\n  retroactively prove earlier stages.\n- **VDS-R2:** Chat / agent narrative is **never** evidence. Evidence must be\n  re-runnable footprints (object ids, job ids, log paths, commit SHAs, CI URLs).\n- **VDS-R3:** Stage advance is forbidden until all chunks for that stage have\n  `independent_verify=yes` **or** a human-authored `waiver_ref`.\n- **VDS-R4:** Customization may change **how** checks execute, never **whether**\n  gates exist.\n\n### Hard gates\n\n- `independent_verify` must be `yes` (not `na`) unless `waiver_ref` is set.\n- Waivers are **human-only**, recorded as durable objects, and reviewable.\n- Orchestrators (CAP, priority plans, release checklists, merge bots) MUST refuse\n  advance/merge/close when in-scope VDS chunks are unverified.\n\n### Forbidden theater\n\n- Narrative-only “done”\n- Empty receipts/matrices without evidence footprints\n- Fabricated health/metrics to force green\n- Closing BLI/CVS/CAP stages without VDS evidence for in-scope work\n- Using customization files to delete stages or hard gates\n\n## Customization (MAY vary by project)\n\nDeclared only in the project’s `verifiable_decomposition_customization.yaml`\n(or equivalent path referenced by the spine profile):\n\n- Code style / lint / formatter commands  \n- Test execution preference: `scheduler` | `foreground` | `ci` | `hybrid`  \n- Process-data mutation: `cli_only` | `allow_direct`  \n- CI required check names, security scanners, performance budgets  \n- Auto-merge conditions and waiver authority  \n\nDefaults for **this** repository are pre-filled (scheduler-first tests, CLI-only\nprocess data, fail-closed public publish). Other projects copy the template and\nfill their own commands — they keep the same five stages and chunk contract.\n\n## Rubric / DSL\n\nEach chunk MUST link a `rubric_ref` (criteria id, matrix row, or rubric anchor) and\none or more machine predicates from the DSL catalog in\n`VERIFIABLE_DECOMPOSITION_SPINE.md` (e.g. `object_exists`, `lint_ok_per_customization`,\n`tests_ok_per_customization`). Projects may add predicates; they may not ship chunks\nwith empty `dsl_checks`.\n\nPrefer binding chunks to a native `verification_matrix` (matrix-driven accountability)\nwhen available.\n\n## Relationship to other policies\n\n- Complements **POL-WORKFLOW-CAP** (CAP consumes VDS evidence; does not replace VDS).  \n- Complements matrix accountability / POL-AGENT-003-style verification_matrix rules.  \n- Complements convergence_session discipline for hypothesis loops.  \n- Does not weaken security, code-quality, or publish fail-closed policies.\n\n## Agent obligations (before saying done)\n\n1. Name stage + `chunk_id`(s).  \n2. Show `rubric_ref` + `dsl_checks`.  \n3. Show `evidence_refs` another party can re-check.  \n4. Confirm `independent_verify` or human `waiver_ref`.  \n\nMissing any item ⇒ work is **not done**. Silence is preferable to false completion.\n\n## Init for a new project\n\n1. Activate this policy (or import equivalent).  \n2. Copy spine profile + customization template.  \n3. Fill customization before first `implement` chunk.  \n4. Wire CAP/CVS/CI as consumers of VDS evidence when those tools exist.\n","category":"workflow","command":"object get","created_at":"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z","created_by":"ACC-1785920548450214012-68b850c0","effective_date":"2026-08-02","enforcement":{"automated":true,"reminder_enabled":true,"review_required":true,"severity":"critical"},"examples":["Valid implement chunk (scheduler customization): claim \"retention deletes base_metric overflow\";\nrubric_ref=CRIT-…; dsl_checks=tests_ok_per_customization;lint_ok_per_customization;\nevidence_refs=SCH-run-…;.zqk/logs/scheduler/test-bundles/…; independent_verify=yes.\n","Invalid: \"Done — steward is working now\" with no chunk_id, no dsl_checks, no job/log evidence.\n"],"id":"POL-WORKFLOW-VDS","kind":"policy","namespace_id":"zqk:kernel","policy_type":"standard","related_object_refs":["GLS-1785637392058851000-6659f7a9","GLS-1785637405161550000-01091b92","GLS-1785637406673432000-2a625c80","BLI-1785637313042867000-cf345687"],"schema_version":"2.0.0","spec":{"category":"process","description":"Mandatory project-agnostic spine: decompose all collaborative work into\nindependently verifiable chunks across intent→design→implement→integrate→operate.\nRigid stages and hard gates; preferences (lint, test runner, style) live in\ncustomization only. Chat claims of done without evidence are violations.\n","enforcement_level":"blocking","rules":[{"description":"One chunk equals one independently verifiable claim; no deferred proof across stages.","id":"VDS-R1"},{"description":"Narrative is never evidence; evidence_refs must be re-runnable footprints.","id":"VDS-R2"},{"description":"Stage advance requires independent_verify=yes for all stage chunks or human waiver_ref.","id":"VDS-R3"},{"description":"Customization may change how checks run, never whether gates exist.","id":"VDS-R4"},{"description":"Orchestrators and merge/close paths must refuse unverified done for in-scope chunks.","id":"VDS-R5"},{"description":"Waivers are human-authored durable objects only; agents must not self-waive.","id":"VDS-R6"},{"description":"Empty dsl_checks or empty evidence_refs is a hard fail for any done claim.","id":"VDS-R7"}],"severity":"critical"},"status":"active","success":true,"title":"Verifiable Decomposition Spine (VDS) — Mandatory Chunked Verification","updated_at":"2026-08-05T09:35:38Z","updated_by":"ACC-1785920548450214012-68b850c0","version_context":"default"}

